{"issue":{"title":"Add padLeft to strutil for zero-padded invoice numbers, and make the README function list complete","problem":"index.js exports capitalize, slugify and truncate. None of them pads a value to a fixed width, so 42 cannot be turned into 00042. The README function list is already incomplete: it has `## capitalize(s)` and `## truncate(s, n)` sections, but slugify is exported from index.js and has no section. test/strutil.test.js covers only capitalize, slugify and truncate.","reason":"Invoice numbers have to be zero padded to a fixed width (42 -> 00042). People look for helpers in the README, so a function missing from it (slugify today, padLeft once added) is hard to find.","outcome":"strutil exports a padLeft function that left-pads a string or number to a given width with a given character, so padLeft(42, 5, '0') gives '00042'. A test covers it. The README has a section for every exported function, including slugify and padLeft.","expect":["index.js exports a function named padLeft, and `node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{if(typeof m.padLeft!=='function')process.exit(1)})\"` exits 0","padLeft(42, 5, '0') returns the string '00042' (a number input is padded)","padLeft('42', 5, '0') returns '00042' and padLeft('7', 3, 'x') returns 'xx7' (a string input is padded with the given character)","padLeft('123456', 5, '0') returns '123456' and padLeft('12345', 5, '0') returns '12345' (input already at or over the width is returned unchanged, not cut)","capitalize, slugify and truncate still return what they did before: capitalize('abc') === 'Abc', slugify(' Hello World! ') === 'hello-world', truncate('abcdef', 4) === 'abc…', truncate('ab', 4) === 'ab'","test/strutil.test.js contains at least one test that calls padLeft, and `npm test` exits 0 with 0 failures","README.md has a `## name(...)` section heading for every function exported from index.js (including slugify and padLeft), and the padLeft section says what its parameters mean"],"proofs":[{"line":"index.js exports a function named padLeft, and `node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{if(typeof m.padLeft!=='function')process.exit(1)})\"` exits 0","proof":"run","how":"node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{if(typeof m.padLeft!=='function')process.exit(1)})\"; echo $?"},{"line":"padLeft(42, 5, '0') returns the string '00042' (a number input is padded)","proof":"run","how":"node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{const r=m.padLeft(42,5,'0');if(r!=='00042'){console.error(r);process.exit(1)}})\""},{"line":"padLeft('42', 5, '0') returns '00042' and padLeft('7', 3, 'x') returns 'xx7' (a string input is padded with the given character)","proof":"run","how":"node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{if(m.padLeft('42',5,'0')!=='00042'||m.padLeft('7',3,'x')!=='xx7')process.exit(1)})\""},{"line":"padLeft('123456', 5, '0') returns '123456' and padLeft('12345', 5, '0') returns '12345' (input already at or over the width is returned unchanged, not cut)","proof":"run","how":"node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{if(m.padLeft('123456',5,'0')!=='123456'||m.padLeft('12345',5,'0')!=='12345')process.exit(1)})\""},{"line":"capitalize, slugify and truncate still return what they did before: capitalize('abc') === 'Abc', slugify(' Hello World! ') === 'hello-world', truncate('abcdef', 4) === 'abc…', truncate('ab', 4) === 'ab'","proof":"run","how":"node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{if(m.capitalize('abc')!=='Abc'||m.slugify(' Hello World! ')!=='hello-world'||m.truncate('abcdef',4)!=='abc…'||m.truncate('ab',4)!=='ab')process.exit(1)})\""},{"line":"test/strutil.test.js contains at least one test that calls padLeft, and `npm test` exits 0 with 0 failures","proof":"run","how":"grep -n 'padLeft(' test/strutil.test.js && npm test"},{"line":"README.md has a `## name(...)` section heading for every function exported from index.js (including slugify and padLeft), and the padLeft section says what its parameters mean","proof":"run","how":"node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>{const r=require('fs').readFileSync('README.md','utf8');const miss=Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function'&&!new RegExp('^## '+k+'\\\\(','m').test(r));if(miss.length){console.error(miss);process.exit(1)}})\" ; then read the padLeft section of README.md to check that it describes the parameters"}],"non_goals":["Adding a padRight or any other new helper","Changing how capitalize, slugify or truncate behave","Publishing a release, bumping the version or deploying anything","Building invoice-number formatting into the invoice service itself"],"assumptions":["Signature is padLeft(s, n, ch): s is the value, n is the target width and ch is the pad character, matching the short parameter style of truncate(s, n)","A number input is converted to its string form before padding, because the example pads the number 42","Input already at or over the width is returned unchanged and is never truncated","The default pad character when ch is left out is the builder's choice (space, like String.prototype.padStart, is reasonable). It is not checked here; tests pass '0' explicitly","Multi-character pad strings and invalid widths (negative, NaN) are not specified and not checked","'Keep the README's list of functions complete' means every exported function, so the slugify section that is missing today must be added too, in the existing `## name(args)` heading style"]}}